542
00:35:08.191 --> 00:35:09.386
Proposed design.

543
00:35:09.666 --> 00:35:19.522
AuthN: an authorization server (or managed IdP) issues OIDC tokens via Code+PKCE for apps and Client Credentials for services.

544
00:35:19.802 --> 00:35:27.866
A gateway validates JWTs (fixed alg, cached JWKS) and passes verified user context downstream.

545
00:35:28.146 --> 00:35:35.165
AuthZ: a shared library calls the policy service for each protected action, always with the object identity.

546
00:35:35.445 --> 00:35:42.207
RBAC for roles, ABAC conditions (store, amount, purpose), ReBAC for ownership or hierarchy.

547
00:35:42.487 --> 00:35:43.511
Default deny.

548
00:35:44.861 --> 00:35:53.053
Service auth: the mesh enforces mTLS with SPIFFE identities; services get dynamic DB creds from the KMS.

549
00:35:53.333 --> 00:36:03.125
Data: an encryption library seals PII fields (AES-256-GCM + KMS-wrapped DEKs, per-tenant KEKs).

550
00:36:03.405 --> 00:36:05.283
Erasure destroys the tenant key.

551
00:36:05.563 --> 00:36:15.845
Assurance: the conformance harnesses (L1, L3 style) run in CI; secret-scanning on commits; periodic pen tests and threat models per feature.

