672
00:46:13.429 --> 00:46:14.431
PKCE.

673
00:46:14.711 --> 00:46:16.226
The rest is in the chapter.

674
00:46:19.076 --> 00:46:19.929
Reading it:

675
00:46:20.209 --> 00:46:25.479
OTP: the naive endpoint answers unlimited wrong guesses, so a 6-digit code falls.

676
00:46:25.759 --> 00:46:35.508
The hardened endpoint locks after 5, caps sends to 3 per 10 minutes, hashes codes at rest with a 5-minute expiry, and compares in constant time.

677
00:46:35.788 --> 00:46:42.167
With a cap of 5 against a million-value space, a blind guess is about 1 in 200,000.

678
00:46:43.517 --> 00:46:53.565
OAuth: the naive or token issues an access token for a wrong PKCE verifier, a missing verifier, and an attacker-controlled redirect URI.

679
00:46:53.845 --> 00:46:57.599
The hardened server enforces the OAuth Security BCP:

680
00:46:57.879 --> 00:47:16.226
S256 PKCE (the verifier must hash to the stored challenge), exact-match registered redirect URIs, and single-use codes, and on a code replay it revokes the token already issued from that code, so an intercepted code that the attacker races on is contained.

