908
01:04:54.803 --> 01:04:56.147
Interview Q and A.

909
01:04:57.397 --> 01:04:58.229
Beginner.

910
01:04:58.509 --> 01:04:59.533
Question 1.

911
01:04:59.813 --> 01:05:03.184
What's the difference between authentication and authorization?

912
01:05:03.464 --> 01:05:04.829
Thirty-second answer:

913
01:05:05.109 --> 01:05:08.651
Authentication proves who you are (login, OTP, certificate).

914
01:05:08.931 --> 01:05:13.112
Authorization decides what you're allowed to do (roles, ownership, policy).

915
01:05:13.392 --> 01:05:19.771
AuthN happens once per session at the edge; authZ must happen on every request and every object.

916
01:05:20.051 --> 01:05:26.856
Confusing them is the root of IDOR: the server checks you're logged in but not that the thing you're accessing is yours.

